An EMPTY stub that replaces the private `duo-streak-daemon` input in the CI.

It exists because Nix fetches ALL the inputs locked in the lock file when evaluating the flake, so
`nix flake check` would demand a read credential for the private repo. With
  nix flake check --override-input duo-streak-daemon path:./ci/stub-duo
the input is swapped BEFORE the fetch and no key enters the CI.

Empty is enough because the only consumer (system/services/duo.nix) uses the input purely as
Docker build CONTEXT (`context: ${duoSrc}`), which is path interpolation, with no readFile at
evaluation time. If the module ever starts READING a file from the repo, the corresponding file
has to exist here (empty) or the check breaks.
